# Add files here to ignore them from prettier formatting.
#
# UNANCHORED, and that is the whole point. `nx format` runs prettier once per
# PROJECT, with the project as the working directory — so a leading slash pins
# a pattern to `packages/<scope>/<name>/`, not to the workspace root, and
# `/dist` matched nothing while every package's own `dist/` was walked. The
# symptom is the same one recorded below: green until a build has run, then
# `nx format:write` exits non-zero on emitted files and writes nothing.
dist
coverage
/.nx/cache
/.nx/workspace-data
.nx/self-healing
/apps/docusaurus/build
/apps/docusaurus/.docusaurus

# Generated at build time and gitignored, so `format:check --all` flags it locally
# (where a build has produced it) but not in CI, where the check runs first — an
# ordering-dependent red main waiting to happen.
/packages/client/ui/.storybook/manager-theme.generated.ts

# The same class, found the hard way: after `build-storybook` and `typecheck`
# have run, these hold thousands of emitted files, and prettier does not merely
# flag them — it EXITS 2 on the ones it cannot parse, so `nx format:write`, the
# command the definition of done tells you to run, fails outright and writes
# nothing. Gitignored is not enough; prettier walks them anyway.
storybook-static
out-tsc

# GENERATED BY `nx release`, and prettier disagrees with every one of them.
# Committing changelogs put 14 of these in the repo, unformatted, in a commit no human wrote
# — and `format:check --all` is a CI gate, so the next push after any release would have been
# red on files nobody touched. Measured on the first release that carried them. A formatter and
# a generator must not both own a file; reformatting them would only move the collision to the
# next release.
CHANGELOG.md
